{"reference":"Luke 23","book":"Luke","chapter":23,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"cultural_context","title":"Responsibility in Luke’s Account","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Luke distributes responsibility for Jesus’ death among several actors: leaders who accuse him, Pilate and Herod, a crowd whose demand prevails, and Roman personnel who carry out the execution. The chapter also portrays dissenting Jewish figures and women who witness these events. This account does not support assigning collective Jewish guilt.","verse_refs":["Luke 23:1-56"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_luke_023_66dfd43427adb16063c56206"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]},{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Questions in the Crucifixion Account","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The words “Father, forgive them” in verse 34 are absent from significant ancient witnesses, so readers should recognize that the sentence’s place in Luke’s original text is disputed. Whether it was original or added early, it neither transfers blame to Jewish people as a whole nor removes accountability from those involved. The chapter’s mercy is still clear in Jesus’ promise to the criminal who appeals to him: “today you will be with me in Paradise.” Later discussions about punctuation and the meaning of Paradise go beyond what the sentence itself settles.","verse_refs":["Luke 23:32-38","Luke 23:39-43","Luke 23:44-56"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_luke_023_62fdbecf1ed82a83248e54f8"],"confidence":"low","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_3","text":"Luke narrates darkness, the torn temple curtain, Jesus’ final prayer, the centurion’s declaration that he was righteous, the crowd’s response, the women’s witness, and Jesus’ burial. These details should first be read in Luke’s own wording rather than being silently reshaped by comparisons with the other Gospels.","verse_refs":["Luke 23:32-38","Luke 23:39-43","Luke 23:44-56"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_luke_023_62fdbecf1ed82a83248e54f8"],"confidence":"low","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}